Here's an example of Go code to calculate daily fiber intake requirement:
```
package main
import "fmt"
func main() {
   age := 30 // age in years
   gender := "male" // "male" or "female"
   calories := 2500 // daily caloric intake
   fiberRequirement := calculateFiberRequirement(age, gender, calories)
   fmt.Printf("Daily fiber intake requirement for a %v-year-old %v with %v calories: %v grams\n", age, gender, calories, fiberRequirement)
}
func calculateFiberRequirement(age int, gender string, calories int) int {
   var fiberRequirement int
   if gender == "male" {
      if age <= 50 {
         fiberRequirement = 38
      } else {
         fiberRequirement = 30
      }
   } else if gender == "female" {
      if age <= 50 {
         fiberRequirement = 25
      } else {
         fiberRequirement = 21
      }
   }
   fiberRequirement = (calories * fiberRequirement) / 1000
   return fiberRequirement
}
```
If the daily fiber intake requirement is not met, it can lead to health consequences such as constipation, digestive problems, increased risk of heart disease, and increased risk of certain cancers. It is important to make sure you are consuming enough fiber in your diet.

