The practical implication of the Butterfly Effect in this scenario is that a small change in the infection rate can have a significant impact on the outcome of the system. For example, if we increase the infection rate to 2.6, the fraction of infected people will grow much faster, and the outcome of the system will be drastically different after 10 days. This demonstrates how small changes in a parameter can lead to large and unpredictable effects on a societal system, such as the spread of a disease.

