Here is a possible implementation of a C# function that retrieves the second longest word from each text using the OpenNLP library and excluding common stop words:
```
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using opennlp.tools.tokenize;
public static string[] GetSecondLongestWords(string textA, string textB)
{
    var tokenizer = new WordTokenizer();
    var stopWords = new HashSet<string> { "the", "and" };
    var wordsA = tokenizer.tokenize(textA).Where(w => !stopWords.Contains(w)).ToList();
    var wordsB = tokenizer.tokenize(textB).Where(w => !stopWords.Contains(w)).ToList();
    var secondLongestA = GetSecondLongestWord(wordsA);
    var secondLongestB = GetSecondLongestWord(wordsB);
    return new[] { secondLongestA, secondLongestB };
}
private static string GetSecondLongestWord(List<string> words)
{
    if (words.Count < 2) return null;
    var longest = words[0];
    var secondLongest = words[1];
    foreach (var word in words.Skip(2))
    {
        if (word.Length > longest.Length)
        {
            secondLongest = longest;
            longest = word;
        }
        else if (word.Length > secondLongest.Length)
        {
            secondLongest = word;
        }
    }
    return secondLongest;
}
```
Here is how the function works:
1. It creates a `WordTokenizer` instance to tokenize the words in the texts.
2. It creates a `HashSet` of stop words that should be excluded from the analysis.
3. It applies the tokenizer to each text and filters out the stop words.
4. It calls the `GetSecondLongestWord` function for each list of words to retrieve the second longest word.
5. The `GetSecondLongestWord` function works by initializing the longest and second longest words to the first two words in the list (assuming there are at least two words).
6. It then iterates over the remaining words in the list and updates the longest and second longest words accordingly.
7. Finally, it returns the second longest word.
Note that the function requires multiple-step reasoning to solve the problem, as it involves tokenization, filtering, and finding the second longest word. It also excludes common stop words to improve the accuracy of the results.

