2. We then extract the sign of `diff` using the right shift operator (`>>`). The sign of `diff` is stored in the most significant bit of the resulting integer. We use a bitwise AND operator (`&`) with the value `0x1` to extract this bit.
3. We then calculate the maximum of the two numbers using the formula `num1 - sign * diff`. If `sign` is 0, then `num1` is greater than `num2`, so we return `num1`. If `sign` is 1, then `num2` is greater than `num1`, so we return `num2`.
Note that this solution assumes that the input numbers are non-negative. If the input numbers can be negative, then the solution needs to be modified to handle two's complement representation of negative numbers.

