    private static String getDefinition(String word) {
        String definition = "";
        JSONParser parser = new JSONParser();
        try {
            Object obj = parser.parse(new FileReader(FILENAME));
            JSONObject jsonObject = (JSONObject) obj;
            if (jsonObject.containsKey(word)) {
                definition = (String) jsonObject.get(word);
            }
        } catch (IOException | ParseException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return definition;
    }
    private static void addDefinition(String word) {
        JSONParser parser = new JSONParser();
        try {
            Object obj = parser.parse(new FileReader(FILENAME));
            JSONObject jsonObject = (JSONObject) obj;
            if (!jsonObject.containsKey(word)) {
                System.out.println("Please enter a definition for " + word + ":");
                String definition = System.console().readLine();
                jsonObject.put(word, definition);
                FileWriter fileWriter = new FileWriter(FILENAME);
                fileWriter.write(jsonObject.toJSONString());
                fileWriter.flush();
                fileWriter.close();
                System.out.println("Definition added successfully.");
            }
        } catch (IOException | ParseException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
    private static String searchDefinition(String word) {
        String definition = "";
        JSONParser parser = new JSONParser();
        try {
            Object obj = parser.parse(new FileReader(FILENAME));
            JSONObject jsonObject = (JSONObject) obj;
            if (jsonObject.containsKey(word)) {
                definition = (String) jsonObject.get(word);
            } else {
                System.out.println(word + " not found in dictionary.");
            }
        } catch (IOException | ParseException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return definition;
    }
}
```
The program uses the `JSON.simple` library to read and write JSON files. The `generateRandomWord()` method generates a random word consisting of 5 characters. The `getDefinition()` method reads the JSON file and returns the definition of a given word if it exists in the file. The `addDefinition()` method prompts the user to enter a definition for a given word and adds it to the JSON file. The `searchDefinition()` method searches for a given word in the JSON file and returns its definition if it exists.
To use the program, simply run the `main()` method. The program will generate a random word and its definition, print them to the console, and prompt the user to enter a definition for the word. After the user enters a definition, the program will save it to the JSON file. Finally, the program will search for the definition of a given word and print it to the console.

