The example code you provided is already a very efficient way to validate a string with exactly 5 numerical digits using regex in PHP. The regular expression pattern `"/^\d{5}$/"` matches a string that starts with the beginning of the line `^`, followed by exactly 5 digits `\d{5}`, and ends with the end of the line `$`. This pattern ensures that the input string contains only 5 numerical digits and nothing else.
If you want to make the code more concise, you can use the shorthand character class `\d` instead of `[0-9]` to match any digit, and you can also use the ternary operator to make the code more compact:
